## Source and binaries ##
The source code is obtained from [Seltha](http://seltha.net/tfe/). The TFE Classic Starter kit was modified minimally to get the code to compile on the following machine:
Linux server 2.6.18-308.8.2.el5.centos.plus #1 SMP Tue Jun 12 15:41:32 EDT 2012 x86_64 x86_64 x86_64 GNU/Linux
using c++ (GCC) 4.1.2 20080704 (Red Hat 4.1.2-52)




## Building (modern-build branch) ##
TFE needs a 32-bit build (`-m32`): its scripting engine keeps pointers in `int`.
`make -C src` works with GCC 8 to 14 when the 32-bit glibc and libstdc++
headers are installed (Fedora: `gcc-c++ make glibc-devel.i686 libstdc++-devel.i686`).

`./build.sh` builds `tfe`, `daemon` and an RPM in Podman images (`tfe-base`,
`tfe-build`) into `dist/`. `./build.sh -u` runs a smoke test first (boot the
world, log in as TempImm, shut down from in game); `-b ubi8|ubi9` picks the
builder base; `-r` rebuilds the images. See `./build.sh --help`.

To run by hand, the binaries must be started from a directory beside the data
(`bin/` next to `area/`, `files/`, `player/`, ...), since every path is
`../<dir>/`; see the directory list in `packaging/tfe.tmpfiles`.
The RPM installs `tfe.service` (disabled), running as user `tfe` in
`/var/lib/tfe/bin`, with settings in `/etc/tfe/tfe.env`.
